{"toolCallId":"call_8f871dc884b548c7bf32cf7681019e0d","title":"Ran grep, echo","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"grep -n \"YOUR_VALUE_HERE\" specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md; echo \"GREP_EXIT=$?\"; echo \"=== impl summary head ===\"; sed -n '1,25p' specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/implementation-summary.md","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"grep -n \"YOUR_VALUE_HERE\" specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md; echo \"GREP_EXIT=$?\"; echo \"=== impl summary head ===\"; sed -n '1,25p' specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/implementation-summary.md","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["grep","echo"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_9b57e13beb634c78bbf81628cd78b28e","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n<!-- FILL: Keep the prefix table and add the two shell variables this task list uses. GOOD: `R` is `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. `A` is `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Variables are defined below. -->\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n<!-- FILL: Replace the sample tasks with the real setup steps. Each task names a file and a verify command. GOOD: T001 Confirm `logs/archive/` holds 10 archives. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: T001 Set up the project. -->\n\n- [ ] T001 Create project structure (`<folder>`). Verify: `ls <folder>` lists it.\n- [ ] T002 Install dependencies (`<manifest>`). Verify: `<install command>` exits 0.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Configure development tools (`<config>`). Verify: `<tool> --version` exits 0.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n<!-- FILL: Write one implementation task per file change. Add a `Verify:` line with the command and its expected output. GOOD: T002 Add the `--keep <n>` branch. Verify: `--keep 3` leaves 3 archives. WEAK: T002 Implement the feature. -->\n\n- [ ] T004 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 1]\n- [ ] T005 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 2]\n- [ ] T006 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Implement core feature 3]\n- [ ] T007 [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Add error handling]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3 and 10. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n\n- [ ] T008 Test happy path manually (`<file>`). Verify: `<command>` prints <expected output>.\n- [ ] T009 Test edge cases (`<test>`). Verify: `<test command>` exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Update documentation (`<doc>`). Verify: `rg -n '<term>' <doc>` prints one line.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n<!-- FILL: Keep the three completion lines and add the one artifact that proves the phase is done. GOOD: `--keep 3` leaves 3 archives and the suite passes. WEAK: Work is complete. -->\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n<!-- FILL: Name the spec and plan files. Add the decision record when the packet has one. GOOD: Specification: `spec.md`. Plan: `plan.md`. WEAK: See the other docs. -->\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `C` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `F` is the 80% fixture folder described in `plan.md` section 5, built under `$TMPDIR`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Record the baseline report from the unmodified script (`C`). Verify: `bash C specs/system-speckit/026-graph-and-context-optimization > /tmp/baseline.txt` exits 0 and `grep 'Overall Completion' /tmp/baseline.txt` prints `Overall Completion: 100%`.\n- [ ] T002 Confirm the script parses cleanly before the change (`C`). Verify: `bash -n C` exits 0.\n- [ ] T003 Build the 80% fixture (`$TMPDIR/min-percent-fixture/spec.md`). Verify: `bash C \"$F\"` prints `Overall Completion: 80%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Declare the option global (`C`). Add `MIN_PERCENT=\"\"` beside `VERBOSE`, `JSON_OUTPUT` and `QUALITY_CHECK` in section 3, so `set -u` never sees it unset.\n- [ ] T005 Add the argument branch (`C`). In the section 8 `case \"$1\"` block, add `--min-percent` that consumes `$2` and rejects a missing value with `ERROR: --min-percent requires a value` on stderr and exit 1; validate the value is an integer from 0 to 100 and reject anything else with `ERROR: --min-percent must be an integer between 0 and 100` and exit 1. Verify: `bash C --min-percent abc \"$F\"` prints the error and exits 1.\n- [ ] T006 Add the threshold comparison (`C`). After the `output_json` / `output_text` call and before the final `exit 0`, compare the reported percentage against `MIN_PERCENT` only when `MIN_PERCENT` is non-empty, exiting 3 when the report is below it. Use `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the stats-file `percentage` in `--file` mode. Verify: `bash C --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` exits 3.\n- [ ] T007 Document the option in `show_help` (`C`). Add `--min-percent <N>` with the 0-100 range and the exit-3 meaning. Verify: `bash C --help | grep -- '--min-percent'` prints one line.\n- [ ] T008 Extend the trailing exit-code comment (`C`). Add `3 - Overall Completion below --min-percent` under the existing `0` and `1` entries. Verify: `tail -5 C | grep -c '3 -'` prints `1`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T009 Syntax check (`C`). Verify: `bash -n C` exits 0.\n- [ ] T010 Below-threshold run (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 90 \"$F\"` exits 3 and still prints the full report including `Overall Completion: 80%`.\n- [ ] T011 At-or-above-threshold run (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 70 \"$F\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T012 Plain run unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C \"$F\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T013 Text output unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `diff <(bash C \"$F\") <(bash C --min-percent 70 \"$F\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T014 JSON output unchanged (`C`, `F`). Verify: `diff <(bash C --json \"$F\") <(bash C --json --min-percent 70 \"$F\")` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T015 Invalid values rejected (`C`, `F`). Verify: `bash C --min-percent 101 \"$F\"`, `bash C --min-percent abc \"$F\"` and `bash C --min-percent` each exit 1 and print no report.\n- [ ] T016 `--file` mode threshold (`C`, `F/spec.md`). Verify: `bash C --file \"$F/spec.md\" --min-percent 90` exits 3 and `--min-percent 70` exits 0.\n- [ ] T017 Update documentation (`spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] `diff` of plain-run stdout against `--min-percent` stdout is empty in both text and `--json` modes\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":20,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":19}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
