{"toolCallId":"call_f82948ecac25444d8afda3e54bc8b127","title":"Wrote ./specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n<!-- FILL: Fill the stack row and write three sentences: what changes, where, and how you will prove it. GOOD: Change one bash script. Add one `--keep <n>` option. Prove it with an archive count. WEAK: This plan describes the implementation. -->\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., TypeScript, Python 3.11] |\n| **Framework** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., React, FastAPI] |\n| **Storage** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., PostgreSQL, None] |\n| **Testing** | [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: e.g., Jest, pytest] |\n\n### Overview\n[2-3 sentences: what this implements and the technical approach]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n<!-- FILL: Turn each gate into a check a command can answer. Keep the boxes unticked until they pass. GOOD: `ls scripts/rotate-logs.sh` prints the path and `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10 before the task starts. WEAK: The team agrees the plan is ready. -->\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [ ] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [ ] Success criteria measurable\n- [ ] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: The test command and the output it must print]\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n<!-- FILL: Name the pattern in three words, then list the one component that changes. GOOD: Single script branch. The component is `scripts/rotate-logs.sh`. WEAK: Standard architecture. -->\n\n### Pattern\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: MVC | MVVM | Clean Architecture | Serverless | Monolith | Other]\n\n### Key Components\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 1]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n- **[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Component 2]**: [YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Purpose]\n\n### Data Flow\n[YOUR_VALUE_HERE: Brief description of how data moves through the system]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n<!-- FILL: Point to `tasks.md` and name the three phases in one line. GOOD: Setup counts the archives. Implementation adds `--keep`. Verification counts 3. WEAK: See tasks. -->\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n<!-- FILL: Name the one command you will run and the output it must print. GOOD: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3 after `--keep 3` and 10 after a plain run. WEAK: Test it manually. -->\n\nN/A — record any testing beyond the verification tasks in `tasks.md` here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: List each tool the change needs, or write `None`. GOOD: `bash` and `awk`. No new package. WEAK: Usual dependencies. -->\n\nN/A — record dependencies beyond the components named in the architecture here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n<!-- FILL: Name the trigger and the one command that reverts the change. GOOD: Trigger: `--keep 3` removes an archive newer than the three kept. Revert the one commit. WEAK: Roll back if needed. -->\n\nN/A — record rollback steps beyond reverting the scoped change here.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add one option to one Bash script: parse --min-percent <N>, keep the existing report untouched, and turn the reported percentage into exit 3 or 0 after the output is printed.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent plan\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: plan-core | v2.4 -->\n# Implementation Plan: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n## 1. SUMMARY\n\n### Technical Context\n\n| Aspect | Value |\n|--------|-------|\n| **Language/Stack** | Bash 3.2-compatible shell |\n| **Framework** | None - a single CLI script |\n| **Storage** | None |\n| **Testing** | Manual CLI invocations plus `bash -n`; the script has no test suite |\n\n### Overview\nOne file changes: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. The argument loop gains a `--min-percent <N>` branch that stores and validates an integer, the existing output functions stay untouched, and a comparison after the report turns the reported percentage into exit 3 or exit 0. Proof is a pair of runs on a fixture that reports 80%, one above the threshold and one below, plus a `diff` showing stdout is unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n## 2. QUALITY GATES\n\n### Definition of Ready\n- [x] Problem statement clear and scope documented\n- [x] Success criteria measurable\n- [x] Dependencies identified\n\n### Definition of Done\n- [ ] All acceptance criteria met\n- [ ] `bash -n .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` exits 0\n- [ ] On an 80% fixture, `--min-percent 90` exits 3 and `--min-percent 70` exits 0\n- [ ] `diff` of plain-run stdout against `--min-percent` stdout is empty, in text and `--json` modes\n- [ ] Docs updated (spec/plan/tasks)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:quality-gates -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:architecture -->\n## 3. ARCHITECTURE\n\n### Pattern\nSingle script, argument switch.\n\n### Key Components\n- **Argument loop (section 8)**: the `while [[ $# -gt 0 ]]` / `case \"$1\"` block that already parses `--verbose`, `--json`, `--quality`, `--file` and `--help`; it gains the `--min-percent` branch and owns N's validation.\n- **Percentage producers**: `calculate_spec_completeness` sets `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` for a folder, and `calculate_file_completeness` writes `percentage` into the per-file stats file; both already finish before any output.\n- **Output functions**: `output_text` and `output_json`; neither changes, which is what keeps stdout byte-identical.\n- **Threshold check**: a new block after the output call and before the final `exit 0`, comparing the reported percentage against `MIN_PERCENT`.\n\n### Data Flow\nThe argument loop stores `MIN_PERCENT` while the folder or file is calculated, the calculation writes `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` (or the stats-file `percentage` for `--file`), the output function prints the report exactly as today, and only then does the threshold block compare the reported percentage with `MIN_PERCENT` and choose exit 3 or exit 0. Because the comparison runs last, a below-threshold run still prints its full report.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:architecture -->\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phases -->\n## 4. IMPLEMENTATION PHASES\n\nFollow the ordered tasks in `tasks.md`. It owns the Setup, Implementation and Verification phase checkboxes and task state.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phases -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n## 5. TESTING STRATEGY\n\nThere is no test suite for this script, so verification is a fixture plus the invocations recorded in `tasks.md`. Build a fixture whose report reads `Overall Completion: 80%` (one `[TODO: ...]` line in five content lines) and assert: `--min-percent 90` exits 3, `--min-percent 70` exits 0, no option exits 0, and `diff` between the plain run and each option run is empty. Repeat the `diff` with `--json` to cover the second output path, and run `bash -n` for syntax.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n## 6. DEPENDENCIES\n\n`bash` 3.2 or newer and `bc`, both already required by the script today; no new package. The `--help` text and the trailing exit-code comment live in the same file, so no documentation outside the script changes.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:dependencies -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:rollback -->\n## 7. ROLLBACK PLAN\n\nTrigger: any caller reports that a plain run changed its output or that exit 3 fires on a complete packet. Roll back by reverting the single commit that touches `calculate-completeness.sh`; the option has no persisted state, so nothing else needs undoing.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:rollback -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":21,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":25}}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/plan.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"write"}}
